{"parentUuid":"f7740973-e2a6-4ada-97d0-1a2a7d7c7c67","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a21d52add52be96a7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WMmD1LcSvojsRdqgP72k5P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MSPKieJonAVGW7jKQLVisj","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"multigrid coarsening combinatorial optimization placement grid problem"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8018,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":348,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8018},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":348,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8018,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caorehns1V9FDnF57sGw9","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"29cf11d9-e29f-4e32-a5e9-f54d470dc0e7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:35.390Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7145b56d-07ac-45e3-8a25-5bab04271f79","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a21d52add52be96a7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TQcAi8KJrKqA1S5Z1RE2M9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"curriculum learning combinatorial optimization survey 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2409.00075] A survey on combinatorial optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.00075\"},{\"title\":\"Machine learning for combinatorial optimization: A methodological tour d’horizon\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/ejores/v290y2021i2p405-421.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"},{\"title\":\"Neural combinatorial optimization with reinforcement learning in industrial engineering: a survey | Artificial Intelligence Review | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10462-024-11045-1\"},{\"title\":\"A survey on combinatorial optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.00075v1\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - dongjinkun/COPZoo: Neural Combinatorial Optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dongjinkun/COPZoo\"},{\"title\":\"Neural Networks for Combinatorial Optimization: A Review of More Than a Decade of Research | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.11.1.15\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding Curriculum Learning in Policy Optimization for Online Combinatorial Optimization | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=gKEbBKRUjA\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] A Survey on Reinforcement Learning for Combinatorial Optimization | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/A-Survey-on-Reinforcement-Learning-for-Optimization-Yang-Whinston/97e4af1c188ad03d822f28dffade5f47f279c619\"},{\"title\":\"Accepted: 29 November 2024 / Published online: 14 February 2025\",\"url\":\"https://d-nb.info/1368674348/34\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found several relevant resources on combinatorial optimization and related topics from 2024-2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## Recent Survey Papers and Research\n\nA recent comprehensive survey investigates the application of reinforcement learning (RL) to solve hard combinatorial optimization (CO) problems, such as vehicle routing, bin packing, assignment, scheduling, and planning problems, and summarizes the applications of neural combinatorial optimization with reinforcement learning (NCO-RL). This survey was published in February 2025 in Artificial Intelligence Review.\n\nAnother survey from August 2024 revisits classical combinatorial optimization algorithms and extends them to two-stage stochastic models, particularly focusing on client-element problems.\n\n## Recent Developments in Neural Combinatorial Optimization\n\nThe field has seen significant activity in 2024-2025. Recent work includes diffusion model frameworks for unsupervised neural combinatorial optimization (ICML 2024), benchmarking for machine learning on classic combinatorial problems (NeurIPS 2025), and large language models as end-to-end combinatorial optimization solvers (NeurIPS 2025).\n\n## Curriculum Learning in Combinatorial Optimization\n\nResearch has presented the first systematic study on policy optimization methods for online combinatorial optimization problems, showing that online CO problems can be naturally formulated as latent Markov Decision Processes (LMDPs), with convergence bounds proven on natural policy gradient (NPG) for solving LMDPs.\n\nThe search results show an active research area with multiple surveys and novel approaches combining machine learning, reinforcement learning, and classical optimization techniques for solving combinatorial problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9792863f-e7d6-4a88-b769-9a8d44e94cce","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:39.157Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7145b56d-07ac-45e3-8a25-5bab04271f79","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"25f088aa-e048-4d32-a7f6-aadbc44a0e91","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a21d52add52be96a7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QaCEoEuAGqWFEUFRX3gEtn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Toenshoff 2020 GNN Max-CSP RUN-CSP scaling generalization larger instances\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Graph Neural Networks for Maximum Constraint Satisfaction Jan Toenshoﬀ\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1909.08387\"},{\"title\":\"Frontiers | Graph Neural Networks for Maximum Constraint Satisfaction\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/artificial-intelligence/articles/10.3389/frai.2020.580607/full\"},{\"title\":\"RUN-CSP/evaluate_weighted_max_cut.py at master · toenshoff/RUN-CSP\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/toenshoff/RUN-CSP/blob/master/evaluate_weighted_max_cut.py\"},{\"title\":\"A Benchmark for Maximum Cut: Towards\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2406.11897\"},{\"title\":\"Graph Neural Networks for Maximum Constraint Satisfaction - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7959828/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - toenshoff/RUN-CSP\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/toenshoff/RUN-CSP\"},{\"title\":\"Beyond-mean-field fluctuations for the solution of constraint satisfaction problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.10360\"},{\"title\":\"Scaling Graph-based Deep Learning models to larger networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.01261\"},{\"title\":\"Chapter 6 Graph Neural Networks: Scalability\",\"url\":\"https://graph-neural-networks.github.io/static/file/chapter6.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Optimization and Reasoning with Graph ...\",\"url\":\"https://jmlr.org/papers/volume24/21-0449/21-0449.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the Toenshoff 2020 paper on GNN approaches for Max-CSP. Here are the key findings:\n\n## RUN-CSP: Graph Neural Networks for Maximum Constraint Satisfaction\n\nThe paper presents a generic graph neural network (GNN) based architecture called RUN-CSP (Recurrent Unsupervised Neural Network for Constraint Satisfaction Problems).\n\n### Scaling and Generalization to Larger Instances\n\nThe paper demonstrates strong results regarding generalization and scalability:\n\n- RUN-CSP networks trained on small random instances generalize well to other instances with larger size and different structure.\n\n- The approach is very efficient and inference takes a few seconds, even for larger instances with over 10,000 constraints.\n\n- The runtime scales linearly in the number of constraints.\n\n### Performance Results\n\nFor specific Max-CSP problems:\n\n- On larger instances it outperforms conventional methods, and training on random instances generalized well to the structured spin-glass instances.\n\n- On graph coloring tasks, the small model achieved 64% on the medium test set and the large model achieved 74% on the small test set, almost matching the performance of the network trained on graphs of the respective size.\n\nThe code for RUN-CSP including the generated datasets and their generators can be found on github.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1d157355-3389-4153-8d36-663ee6782373","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:41.487Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"25f088aa-e048-4d32-a7f6-aadbc44a0e91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"29cf11d9-e29f-4e32-a5e9-f54d470dc0e7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a21d52add52be96a7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MSPKieJonAVGW7jKQLVisj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"multigrid coarsening combinatorial optimization placement grid problem\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Optimization-Based Algebraic Multigrid Coarsening Using Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2106.01854\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization and coarse-grid selection for algebraic multigrid\",\"url\":\"https://memorial.scholaris.ca/items/266ef45b-b38b-43b6-ae1a-be1ad23faeaf\"},{\"title\":\"Multigrid method - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multigrid_method\"},{\"title\":\"Coarse-grid selection using simulated annealing - Luke Olson\",\"url\":\"http://lukeo.cs.illinois.edu/files/2023_ZaMaOlWe_cgselection.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"UCRL-JRNL-220851 An Introduction to Algebraic Multigrid R. D. Falgout\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/897960\"},{\"title\":\"[2105.13280] Coarse-Grid Selection Using Simulated Annealing\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.13280\"},{\"title\":\"Multigrid Solvers and Multilevel Optimization Strategies | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-1-4757-3748-6_1\"},{\"title\":\"Coarse-Grid Selection for Parallel Algebraic Multigrid ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/293405\"},{\"title\":\"Multigrid Methods Volker John Winter Semester 2013/14\",\"url\":\"https://www.wias-berlin.de/people/john/LEHRE/MULTIGRID/multigrid.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A Greedy Strategy for Coarse-Grid Selection | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220411407_A_Greedy_Strategy_for_Coarse-Grid_Selection\"}]\n\nI've found comprehensive information about multigrid coarsening and combinatorial optimization related to grid placement problems. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overview\n\nAlgebraic multigrid (AMG) methods are used when the discretization lacks the structure needed to enable more efficient geometric multigrid techniques.\n\n## The Combinatorial Optimization Problem\n\nA constrained combinatorial optimization problem is used to define the \"best\" coarse grid within the setting of a two-level reduction-based algebraic multigrid method and is shown to be NP-complete. This creates a significant computational challenge for optimal coarse-grid selection.\n\n## Key Algorithmic Approaches\n\n**Coarse-Grid Selection:** A key step in all AMG approaches is the choice of the coarse/fine partitioning, aiming to balance the convergence of the iteration with its cost.\n\n**Solution Methods:** A new coarsening algorithm based on simulated annealing has been developed to approximate solutions to this problem, which yields improved results over the greedy algorithm developed previously.\n\n**Machine Learning Approaches:** Reinforcement learning methods have been developed to achieve scalable (linear order in graph size) and high-quality fine-coarse partitioning, focusing on discretizations of the 2D Poisson equation.\n\n## Problem Characteristics\n\nThe optimization problem is tightly coupled, so that selecting one node to be in the coarse problem affects the eligibility of its neighbouring nodes for selection.\n\nThe search results show active research in this area, with recent work combining optimization techniques with machine learning to solve these computationally challenging grid placement problems efficiently.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1eef0d6b-fce3-424a-9002-ed6d45dce11c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:41.544Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"29cf11d9-e29f-4e32-a5e9-f54d470dc0e7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f7740973-e2a6-4ada-97d0-1a2a7d7c7c67","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a21d52add52be96a7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J2Bt3DWaq51oHZ6cfya5oM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Nair 2021 Neural Diving DeepMind large MIP scaling training data\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Solving Mixed Integer Programs Using Neural Networks | DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.com/research/publications/2021/Solving-Mixed-Integer-Programs-Using-Neural-Networks\"},{\"title\":\"[2012.13349] Solving Mixed Integer Programs Using Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.13349\"},{\"title\":\"Abstract - IPAM\",\"url\":\"http://www.ipam.ucla.edu/abstract/?tid=17001&pcode=DLC2021\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-deepmind/neural_lns · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/neural_lns\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Mixed Integer Programs Using Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"http://helper.ipam.ucla.edu/publications/dlc2021/dlc2021_17001.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"DeepMind & Google Use Neural Networks to Solve Mixed Integer Programs | Synced\",\"url\":\"https://syncedreview.com/2021/08/03/deepmind-podracer-tpu-based-rl-frameworks-deliver-exceptional-performance-at-low-cost-74/\"},{\"title\":\"DeepMind & Google Use Neural Networks to Solve Mixed Integer Programs | by Synced | SyncedReview | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/syncedreview/deepmind-google-use-neural-networks-to-solve-mixed-integer-programs-bf41e3521950\"},{\"title\":\"Learning a Large Neighborhood Search Algorithm for Mixed Integer Programs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2107.10201\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Mixed Integer Programs Using Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/347880794_Solving_Mixed_Integer_Programs_Using_Neural_Networks\"},{\"title\":\"Deepmind uses neural network to automatically construct heuristic algorithm to solve MIP problem\",\"url\":\"https://cdmana.com/2021/08/20210815171805664S.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about the Nair 2021 research on Neural Diving and large-scale MIP solving:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe paper \"Solving Mixed Integer Programs Using Neural Networks\" by Vinod Nair and 18 other authors presents two neural network-based components called Neural Diving and Neural Branching for use in a MIP solver.\n\n## Neural Diving\n\nNeural Diving learns a deep neural network to generate multiple partial assignments for integer variables, and the resulting smaller MIPs for un-assigned variables are solved with SCIP to construct high quality joint assignments.\n\n## Large-Scale Data\n\nThe approach was evaluated on six diverse real-world datasets, including two Google production datasets and MIPLIB, with most instances in all the datasets combined having 10³-10⁶ variables and constraints after presolve, which is significantly larger than previous learning approaches.\n\n## Training Data Approach\n\nThe team trains a deep neural network to produce multiple partial assignments of the integer variables, with the model trained to assign higher probability to feasible assignments with better objective values, and learns on all available feasible assignments.\n\n## Performance Results\n\nComparing solvers with respect to primal-dual gap averaged over a held-out set of instances, the learning-augmented SCIP is 2× to 10× better on all datasets except one on which it is 10⁵× better at large time limits, and this was the first learning approach to demonstrate such large improvements over SCIP on both large-scale real-world application datasets and MIPLIB.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"03b38e9f-a355-4577-b246-6333072d22bb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:43.540Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f7740973-e2a6-4ada-97d0-1a2a7d7c7c67","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D: