{"parentUuid":"9f7c1285-c8ee-40a7-9114-2bbe7d7a92a2","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a21d52add52be96a7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01RyeD68HvN8g9K1W8x8bdPU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0127CWoXzGLQpT9oYrfRjwLo","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"warm start\" CP-SAT phase saving restart rectangle packing previous solution"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5652,"cache_read_input_tokens":32721,"output_tokens":216,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5652},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":216,"cache_read_input_tokens":32721,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5652,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5652,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaorheYywQs9qFHRabEKs","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"404b0561-e817-458d-9555-a8a4791917ce","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:13.466Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9f7c1285-c8ee-40a7-9114-2bbe7d7a92a2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a21d52add52be96a7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BmDPDp9Vmxh4Yqw5TxWywe","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Meta-SAGE scale meta-learning combinatorial optimization scale shift adaptation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2306.02688] Meta-SAGE: Scale Meta-Learning Scheduled Adaptation with Guided Exploration for Mitigating Scale Shift on Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.02688\"},{\"title\":\"Meta-SAGE: Scale Meta-Learning Scheduled Adaptation with Guided Exploration for Mitigating Scale Shift on Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/son23a.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - kaist-silab/meta-sage: [ICML 2023] Meta-SAGE: Scale Meta-Learning Scheduled Adaptation with Guided Exploration for Mitigating Scale Shift on Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/kaist-silab/meta-sage\"},{\"title\":\"Meta-SAGE: Scale Meta-Learning Scheduled Adaptation with Guided\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/son23a/son23a.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ICML Poster Meta-SAGE: Scale Meta-Learning Scheduled Adaptation with Guided Exploration for Mitigating Scale Shift on Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/virtual/2023/poster/25138\"},{\"title\":\"meta-sage/README.md at main · kaist-silab/meta-sage\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/kaist-silab/meta-sage/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Google Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=Son%2C+J.%2C+Kim%2C+M.%2C+Kim%2C+H.%2C+Park%2C+J.%2C+2023.+Meta-SAGE%3A+scale+meta-learning+scheduled+adaptation+with+guided+exploration+for+mitigating+scale+shift+on+combinatorial+optimization.+In%3A+International+Conference+on+Machine+Learning.+pp.+32194%E2%80%9332210.\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - dongjinkun/COPZoo: Neural Combinatorial Optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dongjinkun/COPZoo\"},{\"title\":\"Track: Poster Session 1\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/virtual/2023/session/21603\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Meta-SAGE:\n\n## Overview\nMeta-SAGE is a novel approach for improving the scalability of deep reinforcement learning models for combinatorial optimization (CO) tasks.\n\n## Key Components\nThe method adapts pre-trained models to larger-scale problems in test time by suggesting two components: a scale meta-learner (SML) and scheduled adaptation with guided exploration (SAGE).\n\n### Scale Meta-Learner (SML)\nSML transforms the context embedding for subsequent adaptation of SAGE based on scale information.\n\n### Scheduled Adaptation with Guided Exploration (SAGE)\nSAGE adjusts the model parameters dedicated to the context embedding for a specific instance. SAGE introduces locality bias, which encourages selecting nearby locations to determine the next location.\n\n## Performance\nResults show that Meta-SAGE outperforms previous adaptation methods and significantly improves scalability in representative CO tasks.\n\n## Publication\nMeta-SAGE was published in the Proceedings of the 40th International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML 2023). The official implementation is available on GitHub at the KAIST-SILab repository.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3caabf60-be36-4d94-9a35-f48364cfc011","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:19.201Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9f7c1285-c8ee-40a7-9114-2bbe7d7a92a2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"404b0561-e817-458d-9555-a8a4791917ce","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a21d52add52be96a7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0127CWoXzGLQpT9oYrfRjwLo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"warm start\" CP-SAT phase saving restart rectangle packing previous solution\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Warm Start Optimization. Some introduction to the concept of… | by AlainChabrier | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@AlainChabrier/warm-start-optimization-ac73eef189e9\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"How to warm-start a solver — PuLP 3.3.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://coin-or.github.io/pulp/guides/how_to_mip_start.html\"},{\"title\":\"Restart CP-SAT from the current state in the solution process\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/5yh9MDP9neU\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Ultra Rapid Restarts⋆ Shai Haim1 and Marijn Heule2\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~mheule/publications/rapid.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Starting from a solution: MIP starts\",\"url\":\"https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/icos/22.1.0?topic=mip-starting-from-solution-starts\"},{\"title\":\"Priority Matters: Optimising Kubernetes Clusters Usage with Constraint-Based Pod Packing\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2511.08373v1\"},{\"title\":\"Model Presolve, Warmstart and Conflict Refining in CP Optimizer | PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.slideshare.net/PhilippeLaborie/cp-optimizer\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding warm start, CP-SAT, phase saving, restart, rectangle packing, and previous solutions:\n\n## CP-SAT Warm Start Capabilities\n\nThere is no mechanic to fully warm start the search in CP-SAT, according to discussions in the OR-Tools community. However, CP-SAT hints can be used to warm-start the next solve by providing the current assignment.\n\n## Phase Saving and Rapid Restarts\n\nUsing phase-saving and Luby sequences results in solving many more benchmark instances compared to the original version. Heuristics and data structures have become more restart-friendly, which explains the trend towards more rapid restarts in SAT solvers.\n\n## Rectangle Packing with CP-SAT\n\nCP-SAT is good at finding a feasible packing, but incapable of proving infeasibility in most cases, though it can still pack most of the rectangles even for larger instances. For packing problems specifically, certain expensive propagation techniques can significantly speed up the search in packing problems, and can be added to a single subsolver where beneficial workers can share their solutions with the rest of the portfolio.\n\n## General Warm Start Concepts\n\nIn practice, when solving the same model repeatedly with new instances of data, it may help a lot to start from the previous solution.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e0d15eb5-aabe-4575-87a8-80a76cf698ed","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:20.702Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"404b0561-e817-458d-9555-a8a4791917ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e0d15eb5-aabe-4575-87a8-80a76cf698ed","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a21d52add52be96a7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KPsut61AEJm8rfBAHDocQ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material to synthesize. Let me write the report now.\n\n---\n\n# 调研：Curriculum Learning / Progressive Scaling 在大规模组合优化的应用\n\n## 1. 综述（CO 领域 2024-2026）\n\nCurriculum learning 在 CO 领域已成系统方向。最相关的近期工作是 **Enhancing NCO by Progressive Training Paradigm (Neurocomputing 2025)** [link](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0925231225023793)，结论是：先小后大的训练能同时改善 in-distribution 和 OOD 泛化。**NCO-RL Survey (AI Review 2025)** [link](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10462-024-11045-1) 系统总结了路由/打包/调度/分配。**受益**：TSP/CVRP/scheduling/bin-packing（结构平移性强，graph 局部性主导）。**不受益**：硬约束密集且尺寸缩放后约束密度变化大的问题（如 RCPSP-with-tight-makespan、刚性 packing），缩到小规模会让\"挤压度\"变化太大，迁移过来的 hint 反而误导。**对我们：** 70→80 网格放大 + 流水线复杂度 ×2-3 属于\"约束密度变化大\"的危险区，需要先做分布漂移度量。\n\n## 2. Toenshoff 2020 RUN-CSP\n\n[arxiv 1909.08387](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1909.08387) / [Frontiers AI 2020](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/artificial-intelligence/articles/10.3389/frai.2020.580607/full)。RUN-CSP 是 Recurrent Unsupervised GNN，关键发现：**在小随机实例上训，能直接迁移到 10000+ 约束的实例**（runtime 线性）。Coloring 任务上，small model 在 medium test 上 64%，large model 在 small test 上 74%。**架构借鉴**：unsupervised + recurrent（多步消息传递做软分配）。**对我们**：可以把 70×70 的 placement 编码为 CSP 图，用 RUN-CSP 风格 GNN 给出每个 cell 的\"先验占用概率\"，作为 CP-SAT hint。\n\n## 3. Nair 2021 Neural Diving (DeepMind)\n\n[arxiv 2012.13349](https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.13349)。**规模**：10³–10⁶ 变量的真实 MIP（Google 生产 + MIPLIB），SCIP 变快 2×–10×（一个数据集 10⁵×）。**数据采集**：不是先小后大，而是从同分布采\"足够多 feasible 解 + 按目标值加权\"，监督学习。训练成本：用 TPU 集群跑数天到周量级。**对我们的启示**：与其 60→70→80 curriculum，不如在 70×70 尽可能采集 1 万+ 高质量 feasible 解（campaign 已经在产了），训完直接 hint 80×80。但要注意：Neural Diving 的 pre-condition 是 train/test 同分布，跨规模需要额外的 normalization。\n\n## 4. 缩小再放大 / Coarsening / Multi-grid\n\n学术名词：**Algebraic Multigrid (AMG) coarsening** [arxiv 2106.01854](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2106.01854)。把 70×70 合并成 35×35（2×2 cell 合并）属于几何 multigrid。AMG 的核心难点是 coarse-grid selection 是 NP-complete，已有 simulated annealing [arxiv 2105.13280](https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.13280) 和 RL 方法。**对我们**：合并 cell 后 4 邻接关系不变，但设施的\"占地形状\"变成 0.5×0.5 的小数尺寸，需要重定义\"coarse facility footprint\"。可行做法：把 mandatory 设施按聚类合并到 coarse cell，先解 coarse rectangle 给出大区域的占用骨架，再 fine-grid 内部填充——本质就是 VLSI 的 floorplan→detail。\n\n## 5. Transfer Learning 在 CO\n\n[Transfer Learning for VRP](https://imt-mines-ales.hal.science/hal-03717063) / [MDPI 2024](https://www.mdpi.com/1999-4893/17/2/87)。结论：**TSP→CVRP 迁移有效**（结构相似），**TSP→ATSP 迁移效果一般**（约束语义不同）。**70→80 相似度评估**：网格类型、设施集合、目标函数（max area, min_side ≥ 6）若不变，相似度高；若 1.2 引入新设施类型/新约束，等价于 CVRP→VRPTW 这种\"增加新维度\"的迁移，需要在新维度的特征上 finetune。\n\n## 6. Multi-scale 优化（VLSI 借鉴）\n\n[PATOMA hierarchical floorplan](https://home.engineering.iastate.edu/~cnchu/pubs/j53.pdf) / [Multilevel FPGA placement](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11390-010-9389-y)。VLSI 标准范式：**top-down recursive bipartition → leaf rectangle packing → V-cycle 多层 refinement**。**对我们 70×70 网格高度借鉴**：第一层把 70×70 切成 4 个 35×35 象限，每象限独立 master + binding；第二层在边界处 routing 修补。已经和我们的 Benders 分解结构对齐，可以直接做\"双层 Benders\"——外层在 35×35 粗网格做 placement，内层在 70×70 精网格做 routing/flow。\n\n## 7. Self-play / 自博弈\n\n[Self-Improved NCO 2024](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.19561) / [Self-Improvement SI](https://openreview.net/forum?id=agT8ojoH0X) / [Multi-Action SI 2025](https://arxiv.org/html/2510.12273)。范式：**当前模型采样多解 → 取最优当伪标签 → 监督训练下一代**。**算力需求**：单张 GPU 量级即可启动；DeepMind 级别的 multi-agent 加速可降低 50-80% wall-clock。**对我们**：完全可行，campaign 已经在累积 checkpoint，把 checkpoint 当 self-play 数据。\n\n## 8. 针对 80×80 的具体方案\n\n**数据生成**：(a) 把现有 70×70 campaign solution 通过 zero-padding 嵌入 80×80 当锚点（10000+ 已有数据复用率 100%）；(b) 用 35×35 缩放 + 80×80 真实 instance 各占 50% 训练。\n**模型**：**GNN 优于 transformer**——70×70 grid 是天然图结构，graph locality 强；transformer 的 O(N²) attention 在 6400 cell 上太重。具体推 **Heavy Decoder LEHD** [arxiv 2310.07985](https://arxiv.org/html/2310.07985v2)（小训大泛，已实证 100→1000）。\n**Hint 接口**：CP-SAT 用 `model.add_hint(var, value)` ([CP-SAT Primer](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html))。**注意坑**：CP-SAT 只对 complete hint 高效用；partial hint 需先做 quick fix-and-solve 补全；presolve 阶段超时会丢 hint（已知 issue #3750）。\n**预期量化**：70×70 单 wave 当前 168h，加 hint 后参考 Neural Diving 的 2-10× → **30-80h**；80×80 无 hint 估算 500-1000h，加 70→80 迁移 hint 估 **150-400h**。\n\n## 9. 失败模式\n\n- **分布漂移检测**：用 **ASAP Satisficing Generalization Edge** [arxiv 2501.17377](https://arxiv.org/html/2501.17377) 框架，在每个 80×80 instance 上跑 propose-then-select，若 propose 的接受率 < 阈值（例如 30%）就报警。\n- **设施类型变化**：1.2 新设施会让旧 GNN 的 facility embedding 缺位。对策：embedding 表保留 OOV slot，新类型走零向量 + finetune；监控 OOV 占比，超 10% 触发重训。\n- **\"约束密度漂移\"指标**：测 (mandatory_count / grid_area) 和 (port_count / facility_count)；70→80 这两个比例若变化 >20%，curriculum hint 期望失效。\n\n## 10. 纯算法 curriculum（不上 ML）\n\n工程量小、收益直接，**优先做这条**：\n- **60→70→80 candidate 收割**：60×60 解出的\"未占用 region\"直接当 70×70 candidate 的初始集合扩展；70×70 已 prove 不可行的 placement pattern（Benders cut）原样导入 80×80 master 当 nogood。Benders cut 是数学严格的，跨规模安全。\n- **rule-based pattern library**：把 70×70 campaign 中频繁出现的 facility cluster (e.g. \"3 power pole + 2 storage 紧凑布局\") 抽成 pattern，80×80 master 优先以 pattern 为单位下 decision。\n- **工程量估算**：cut 复用 + pattern 抽取 ≈ 1-2 周；ML pipeline ≈ 2-3 月。**ROI 上纯算法 curriculum 完胜**。\n\n---\n\n## 对我们 70→80 升级的具体方案（综合）\n\n**双轨推进**：\n\n**轨 A（必做，1-2 周）**：纯算法 curriculum。①Benders cut 跨规模复用（70 的 nogood → 80 的 nogood，按坐标平移 + 留出 10 cell 边界缓冲）；②高频 facility pattern 抽取，80×80 master 把 pattern 当宏 decision；③双层 Benders：外层 35×35 粗 placement，内层 70×70 fine routing（直接借 VLSI multilevel）。**预期**：80×80 单 wave 从 1000h → 300-500h，且全程 certified_exact。\n\n**轨 B（探索，2-3 月，shadow-only）**：GNN sidecar。①架构选 LEHD heavy decoder + RUN-CSP 风格 message passing；②训练数据 = 70×70 campaign checkpoint + 35×35 coarse 解，self-play 迭代 2-3 代；③输出仅作为 CP-SAT hint，符合 AI 安全契约（order_only / hints not constraints）；④分布漂移用 ASAP propose-then-select 监控，propose 接受率 < 30% 即弃用。**预期**：在轨 A 基础上再降 50% wall-clock，到 **150-250h**。\n\n**关键数字回顾**：\n- LEHD：100 训 → 1000 推泛化良好，对 70→80 这种 1.14× 缩放绰绰有余\n- Neural Diving：2-10× 加速（同分布）\n- RUN-CSP：训小测大泛化 64-74%\n- Meta-SAGE [arxiv 2306.02688](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.02688)：scale shift 自适应专门方案，可作为 sidecar 回退方案\n\n**Sources:**\n- [Enhancing NCO by Progressive Training Paradigm (Neurocomputing 2025)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0925231225023793)\n- [NCO-RL Survey (AI Review 2025)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10462-024-11045-1)\n- [RUN-CSP arxiv 1909.08387](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1909.08387)\n- [RUN-CSP Frontiers AI 2020](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/artificial-intelligence/articles/10.3389/frai.2020.580607/full)\n- [Neural Diving / Solving MIPs with NN (Nair 2021)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.13349)\n- [AMG Coarsening with RL](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2106.01854)\n- [Coarse-Grid Selection via Simulated Annealing](https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.13280)\n- [Transfer Learning for VRP](https://imt-mines-ales.hal.science/hal-03717063)\n- [Transfer RL for CO (MDPI 2024)](https://www.mdpi.com/1999-4893/17/2/87)\n- [PATOMA Hierarchical Floorplan](https://home.engineering.iastate.edu/~cnchu/pubs/j53.pdf)\n- [Multilevel FPGA Placement](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11390-010-9389-y)\n- [Self-Improved Learning for Scalable NCO](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.19561)\n- [Self-Improvement Sample Without Replacement](https://openreview.net/forum?id=agT8ojoH0X)\n- [Multi-Action Self-Improvement](https://arxiv.org/html/2510.12273)\n- [LEHD Heavy Decoder for Large Scale Generalization](https://arxiv.org/html/2310.07985v2)\n- [Meta-SAGE ICML 2023](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.02688)\n- [ASAP Satisficing Generalization Edge](https://arxiv.org/html/2501.17377)\n- [CP-SAT Primer Coding Patterns (hints)](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html)\n- [CP-SAT hint UNKNOWN issue #3750](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750)\n- [Neural TSP Progressive Distillation (AAAI)](https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/26432)\n- [Learn to Reduce Search Space (Routing)](https://arxiv.org/html/2503.03137)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2913,"cache_read_input_tokens":38373,"output_tokens":4928,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2913},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4928,"cache_read_input_tokens":38373,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2913,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoriUpcso4BSgV3Yytkv","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6f5e232f-44a7-4d5d-8f59-44672608ad2b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:48.013Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
